# foritself: S2 takes "for its own sake" as not as a means. S3 gives the reason as the pleasure of being conscious of virtue.
# Critics read that reason as making virtue a means to pleasure. But the text treats the two as the same claim, which is what the argument argues for.
# So I count this as one sense, though I was unsure.
